<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/capacityWeight">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Capacity of the transport element measured by weight. Usually measured in kilograms (kg) or grams (g).</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">capacity weight</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/solarTransmittance">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">(Tsol) The ratio of incident solar radiation that directly passes through a shading system (also named _e). Note the following equation Asol + Rsol + Tsol = 1</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solar transmittance</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/visibleLightReflectance">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fraction of the visible light that is reflected by the glazing at normal incidence. It is a value without unit.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">visible light reflectance</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/supportedWeightMax">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The maximum weight that can be carried by the vibration isolator. Usually measured in kilograms (kg) or grams (g).</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">maximum supported weight</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/solarReflectance">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">(Rsol): The ratio of incident solar radiation that is reflected by a shading system (also named _e). Note the following equation Asol + Rsol + Tsol = 1</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solar reflectance</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/vibrationTransmissibility">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The vibration transmissibility percentage.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">vibration transmissibility</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/thermalTransmittance">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Rate at which energy is transmitted through a body. Usually measured in Watts/m2 Kelvin.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">thermal transmittance</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/isolatorStaticDeflection">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Static deflection of the vibration isolator. Usually measured in millimeters (mm).</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isolator static deflection</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/isolatorCompressibility">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The compressibility of the vibration isolator.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isolator compressibility</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/visibleLightTransmittance">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fraction of the visible light that passes the shading system at normal incidence. It is a value without unit.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">visible light transmittance</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://saref.etsi.org/saref4bldg/height">
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Height of the vibration isolator before tha application of load. Usually measured in millimeters (mm).</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">height</rdfs:label>
</rdf:Description>

